      "writtenOn": "2025-03-10T19:40:00Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The implementation of `LoadLibraryExA` converts the passed in string to wide characters and calls `LoadLibraryExW`. So having this method accept `std::string` means two string conversions, one when calling \"OpenSystemLibrary\" and one when calling the OS. Passing a `std::wstring_view` here eliminates both the copies.\n\nAs a followon change, would be good for us to standardize on wide characters for all of the Windows filepath ingesting code in Dawn. FWIW, Chromium does this.",
      "parentUuid": "21028785_d36bb4f0",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 53,
        "startChar": 27,
        "endLine": 53,
        "endChar": 44
      },
      "revId": "a4fdb6c078ebd29ea6371f52a17ca1643b842eed",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
